{
  "id": "us.bank-statement",
  "version": 1,
  "name": "US Bank Statement",
  "emoji": "🏦",
  "description": "US checking, savings and credit union statements, also business, church and nonprofit accounts, with the check images and deposited items pages. Hides the routing number (after Routing number, ABA, RTN or R/T), the account number in every form: after Account, Acct or Account number, after the product name (Small Business Checking 1234567890, Premier Savings ...4521, Share Draft 0012345678), in page headers and corners, masked (XXXXXX4521, ****4521, ...4521), after ending in, member and customer numbers, the card digits in Card 4521, the MICR line at the bottom of checks and deposit slips as OCR reads it (routing, account and check number), the account holder (any line naming a church, ministry, LLC, Inc., association, foundation or trust, the name after Account name, Account holder, Owner, INDN or For deposit only, and in a PDF the name lines above the mailing address), the street line, P.O. Box, city, state and ZIP, phone numbers, e-mail and SSN or tax ID. Handwritten signatures on the check images are covered by the Signatures detector, which this preset switches on. Keeps amounts, balances, dates, transaction descriptions, check numbers in the lists and under the images, the bank's name and its toll-free and customer service numbers. Limits: the USPS postal barcode and handwriting (payee, memo, endorsements) need a manual box; the bank's own address is covered too by the Addresses detector (remove it with the X), and so is an organization printed on a deposited check; a person's name on its own line of a scan, other people's names and long reference numbers in the descriptions are handled by the Names & Surnames and Account Numbers detectors; a holder's name cut short inside an ACH description is not detected.",
  "language": "en",
  "country": "US",
